// What conformance to a module trait refuses once declarations have types: what
// a conforming module declares under a member's name must have the member's
// shape. A function member is met by a function with its signature, exactly; a
// global member by a global of its type and its permission. That holds for a
// declaration overriding a default as for one meeting a requirement. Each
// difference is reported where the 'is' is written, naming the member.
//
// Type check stage. Each one-file module beside this file conforms to Runner:
//   wrongsig.cone    a function with another parameter type
//   wrongkind.cone   a global where a function is required, and the reverse
//   wrongtype.cone   a required global and an overriding one of another type
//   wrongperm.cone   a required global declared 'imm' where Runner says 'mut'

pub mod trait Runner {
  pub fn step(n i64) i64;
  pub mut scale i64;
  pub mut offset = 100i64;
  pub fn run(n i64) i64 {
    step(n) * scale + offset;
  }
}
